# Registry packages that the bundled skills (internal/tools/skills/data) and
# tools.md tell the agent or an operator to install. Checked by
# TestInstallCommandsNameVerifiedPackages.
#
# The agent follows skill commands on the scanning host, so every name here
# must be one the intended project actually publishes on that registry, with
# releases. Before adding an entry, open the registry page and confirm the
# owner, homepage and release history match the tool the skill means. If the
# project does not publish there under that name, change the skill to the
# project's upstream install method (git clone, go install, distro package)
# instead of adding the name.
#
# Format: <pypi|npm|rubygems|crates> <name>
# PyPI names are PEP 503-normalized (lowercase, runs of - _ . become -);
# crate names are lowercase with _ written as -.

